#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""ci-main-status: is main green, red, or untested? Read before every merge.

usage: ci-main-status [--tip | --merge-gate] REPO     (dotfiles, loop-engine, agent-kit, coordinator, homelab, amazon-itemizer, alert-steward, storycraft, retro, eval-cases, budget-steward)
       ci-main-status [--tip | --merge-gate] --all
       ci-main-status --merge-gate REPO --pr N         (the fix for a red main, below; for eval-cases and budget-steward the PR being merged, below)
       ci-main-status [--merge-gate] OWNER/REPO [--pr N]   (any other GitHub repo: its default branch's required checks)
       ci-main-status --threads REPO PR                (the PR's unresolved review threads, below)

--merge-gate is for `ci-main-status --merge-gate REPO && gh pr merge ...` (playbook fab9b713: only a red main stops a
merge). UNTESTED exits 0 and still prints its UNTESTED line; RED and unreadable still exit 1. Do not use `ci-main-status
REPO; [ $? -le 2 ] && ...` instead: it lets red (1) through. It cannot be combined with --tip (a deploy needs a pass).

--pr N (only with --merge-gate and one REPO) is for the PR that fixes a red main (fab9b713 lets the revert or fix merge into
a red main). Without --pr nothing changes. With it, a red main passes only under the rule for that repo; then the RED lines print as
usual, followed by one "merge-gate:" line, and the exit is 0. Anything else exits 1 with the same stdout as without --pr; the
reason goes to stderr. A red verdict that is not a GitHub run (the coordinator's journal) is always refused.

  Every repo: PR N passes when its own full-suite run on its exact head tree succeeded. That is a run of the same
  workflow whose failure made main red, on PR N's head commit or on a commit with the same tree. It counts only when every job
  that did not pass in main's red run ran in it and passed, and so did each step that failed there. A job or step that was
  skipped does not count: agent-kit's unit.yml skips `npm test` and the node-floor job on pull_request events, so a
  pull_request run is not a full-suite run and a workflow_dispatch run on the branch is. Runs are read newest first: one that
  skipped a red job or step is passed over, and the first one that ran them decides (a failed one refuses). The "merge-gate:"
  line names the run (id and URL). No such run, a failed one, a run still going with its steps listed, a run on another tree or one that skipped a red job refuses.

  dotfiles tries one more rule first (the pin fix), and falls back to the rule above when it does not apply: a red main passes
  as the pin fix when all three hold. (1) The red run's only failing step is the "Release pins: ..." step (a new agent-kit or
  Loop Engine release turned the pin check red; playbook 7c57de5a). (2) PR N changes exactly the pin files: agent-kit's
  package.json and package-lock.json, or the Loop Engine bump's files (the mise config, plus skills under the canonical skills
  tree), or both sets in one combined bump PR. (3) PR N's own pull_request run succeeded and passed that step. A dotfiles red that is not that gets the rule above,
  so its fix passes when its own full-suite run on its head tree passed what failed. When neither rule passes both reasons go to stderr.

--threads REPO PR is the per-PR check the repo-wide gate cannot be: PR PR must have no unresolved review thread (playbook 580f3e02
step 3, "resolve the threads", as a gate; the idea is poteto's watch-pr). REPO is a table name, OWNER/REPO, or a bare name taken as
cartwmic/NAME. GitHub: GraphQL reviewThreads. Every thread that is not resolved counts, outdated ones included (GitHub marks a thread outdated
when the lines under it change, which does not mean the finding was answered): only resolving a thread clears it. Any unresolved one is RED,
exit 1, and each is printed as `path:line  first line of its first comment  url`.
Gitea (budget-steward): the review comments' `resolver` says who resolved a conversation, and every unresolved one counts, the same as on
GitHub. A conversation is the comments on one path and diff position, resolved when any of them has a resolver; two separate conversations at
the same path and position (rare) read as one, so resolving either clears both: Gitea's API gives no id that tells them apart. A read that
fails, or a malformed answer, is ERROR, exit 1: no silent pass. Every run writes one line to ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-~/.local/state}/ci-main-status/threads.jsonl
(CI_MAIN_STATUS_THREADS_LOG overrides it), whoever calls it: ts (UTC), duration_ms, repo, pr, forge (github or gitea), result (pass, refused or
error), unresolved (the count, or null on error), threads (path, line and url of each unresolved thread), exit and detail (the error, on error).
Who runs it: the
`pr-body-check REPO PR` shim runs it after the body check (every merge chain already runs that: the hook's gh pr merge chain, the
homelab merge-pr.sh, the bump scripts), and the Gitea PR gate (`--merge-gate budget-steward --pr N`) runs it itself after its own
evidence passes, as that repo's only merge gate.

A table repo marked no_ci has no CI and cannot have required checks (today eval-cases: a private repo on a plan with no
rulesets or branch protection; GitHub answers 403 "Upgrade to GitHub Pro or make this repository public"). Main has no state
to read, so its merge gate is the PR's own review and body check: `--merge-gate eval-cases --pr N` (or cartwmic/eval-cases)
reads PR N's head from GitHub, then runs `agent-traces review verify --item eval-cases#N --head <head> --require-block`
and `pr-body-check cartwmic/eval-cases N`. Both run, and both exit 0: one "no CI" line naming what it passed on, exit 0.
Either fails: a line for each (the failing one with its reason), exit 1. A missing agent-traces or pr-body-check is a failure
(both are personal-profile tools, so on the work profile this gate exits 1). `--merge-gate eval-cases` without --pr exits 1:
it cannot know which PR is merging, so pass --pr N. Without --merge-gate (plain status, --tip, --all) and with --merge-gate
--all it prints one "n/a (no CI ...)" line and exits 0, like homelab: it never changes the exit of the other repos.
One more no-CI repo is one more REPOS row ({"github": "owner/repo", "no_ci": True}) and its ORDER entry.

A table repo with a "gitea" key lives on the homelab Gitea, not on GitHub (today budget-steward: cartwmic/budget-steward, no CI
runner, no required checks; it is gated on a kgate run, playbook 83fbe006). Gitea has no `gh`, so the script reads the Gitea API
itself (https://gitea.internal.cartwmic.com/api/v1; CI_MAIN_STATUS_GITEA_API overrides it). The token is
CI_MAIN_STATUS_GITEA_TOKEN, else the git credential for the Gitea host (the same helper `git push` uses); never printed. A repo
that is private answers 404 to no token: that is an unreadable state (exit 1), never "no evidence". A Gitea repo is not part of
--all: a machine that cannot reach Gitea (the work Mac, a pod with no token) must not make --all fail; name it to read it. Profiles: the script ships to both; budget-steward is a personal-homelab repo, so the work profile never gates it
(it has no Gitea reach, and the call would exit 1 with an ERROR line).
  Evidence for a commit is the worse of two sources: (1) the Gitea combined commit status (success is a pass, failure or error is a
  fail, no status at all is no evidence); (2) the newest kgate run recorded in ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-~/.local/state}/kgate/log.jsonl
  (CI_MAIN_STATUS_KGATE_LOG overrides it) for the commit's git tree hash (read by a one-commit git fetch: Gitea's API gives the
  commit's own sha as its tree; CI_MAIN_STATUS_GITEA_GIT overrides the fetch URL), of this repo, that ran to its end, was not cancelled and
  ran the full suite (its command holds both `npm run typecheck` and `npm test`; a run of a few proof tests does not count). Exit 0
  is a pass, any other exit a fail. kgate hashes the shipped files the way `git write-tree` does, so a run on a branch that has the
  same tree as the commit counts for the commit.
  `--merge-gate budget-steward --pr N`: reads PR N from Gitea (it must be open and aimed at main) and its head commit, and passes
  (exit 0, one GREEN line naming the evidence) only when the head has a pass and no fail. No evidence is a RED line, exit 1:
  main's own state cannot stand in for it, because a squash merge writes a new tree that no kgate run has seen, so main reads
  UNTESTED forever. Without --pr it exits 1 and says to pass one, like eval-cases. The gate proves the PR head's own tree, not
  the merge result; the squash merge into a main that moved is the merger's to check (Gitea's `head_commit_id` pin does that).
  Plain status and --tip read main's tip the same way: GREEN on a pass (--tip: tip <sha>), RED on a fail, UNTESTED (exit 2)
  with no evidence.
  Every budget-steward call (merge gate, --tip, plain status; a pass, a refusal or an error) appends one JSON line to
  ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-~/.local/state}/ci-main-status/gitea.jsonl (CI_MAIN_STATUS_GITEA_LOG overrides it): ts (UTC), duration_ms,
  action (merge-gate, tip, status), repo, pr, sha, tree, verdict (GREEN, RED, UNTESTED, ERROR), exit (the gate's own code),
  evidence ({"gitea_status": state or null, "kgate_job": id or null}) and detail (the verdict line, token scrubbed). The token is never
  written. The GitHub paths leave their record through the gh wrapper; this path makes no gh call, so it writes its own.

Every table repo's full name (the "github" field of its row: cartwmic/dotfiles, cartwmic/coordinator, StoryCraftTW/storycraft, ...,
matched without regard to case) is its table entry: it gets the same verdict as the short name, including --merge-gate, --pr,
--tip and plain status. So `--merge-gate cartwmic/dotfiles` and `--merge-gate dotfiles` read the same CI run and say the same
thing. (Once the full name took the any-repo path below and read only GitHub's required checks; dotfiles requires only "tests", so
a red run on another job, mise-tests, passed the gate: dotfiles#689 merged into a red main.) The coordinator and eval-cases
have no required checks to read, so for them the any-repo path could only refuse.

Any other GitHub repo, named OWNER/REPO (a name with a slash that is not a table repo's full name): the exact set
of checks GitHub requires to merge into the default branch, from two sources both always read. Classic branch
protection comes from the branch itself (GET repos/.../branches/{b}, read access is enough; it carries
protection.enabled and its required_status_checks to a non-admin, and the classic /protection endpoints —
admin-only, 404 to a non-admin even when protection exists — are never called). The active rulesets that apply to
the branch come from rules/branches (org rulesets included, paged at 100, the branch name URL-encoded). A ruleset
rule type this gate does not know to be check-free (workflows, code_scanning, code_quality, required_deployments,
or any type GitHub adds later) fails closed: ERROR, never GREEN. So do a protected branch with no required checks
in either source, a malformed response, or a read that fails: the full set must be known, never a smaller one and
never "none" unless proven. All of them passed on the tip: GREEN, 0. One failed: RED, 1. One is
queued, running or has not reported: UNTESTED, 2 — and UNTESTED never passes the merge gate for these repos:
--merge-gate exits non-zero on a pending, missing or never-reported required check, where the table repos'
2-becomes-0 does not apply. A required check passes as GitHub's merge box passes it: a completed check run whose
conclusion is success, skipped or neutral (GitHub: required checks need "a successful, skipped, or neutral status").
Per name the newest run decides, the highest check-run id (a newer queued or running run is still newest); a
commit status with the same name is combined in, the worse verdict winning. --pr N (only with --merge-gate)
checks the PR's head commit against the required checks instead of the tip — for a table repo --pr means the fix
for a red main (above); here main is not read. The set the gate verifies on the PR head is the required set
computed for the PR's base branch, never gh pr checks --required's list: that rollup holds only checks present in
the PR, so a required check that never started is missing from it, and a name with no run on the head fails the
gate. gh pr checks --required is a cross-check only: a name it marks required that the computed set lacks is an
ERROR (an under-report); its pending (exit 8) and none-reported (exit 1) states do not end the check, and any
other exit fails closed. When the required checks cannot be read at all (none required, no permission, a rate
limit), it says so and exits 1: no silent pass. --tip is not for these repos (a deploy pulls a sha of a repo on
this machine).

This is not the flake ruling (that is the coordinator's journal) and it is not a bypass of the merge hook, which still needs
`ci-main-status ... && pr-body-check ... && gh pr merge`.

--tip is for deploy. Without it, green means "not red": the newest conclusive commit passed, and untested commits
may sit on top while a run is going. That is right for the merge freeze. With --tip, exit 0 needs main's tip itself
to have a conclusive pass. A green commit below untested commits is 2 even while a run is going (the message says
whether one is). Red is still 1. Everything else is unchanged. The coordinator journal matches by tip sha or by tree (see below), so it
follows the same rule.

Verdicts belong to commits, not to times. The script walks main's first-parent line from the tip, newest first.
A commit's verdict comes from its full-workflow runs on main (push and workflow_dispatch): the highest run id
with a conclusive verdict counts, and a run's verdict is its newest conclusive attempt. Only success and failure
are conclusive; cancelled, skipped and still-running runs are not, and a run still going is reported as "going".
A red run whose rerun (gh run rerun) is going holds its commit red until the rerun ends. Start and created
times are never read.

A failed attempt is untested, not red, when the only jobs in it that did not pass or skip were cancelled because no runner
picked them up (GitHub's annotation on the job's check run: "The job was not acquired by Runner of type hosted even after
multiple attempts"). No test ran, so it is never green and never red. Any real failure, a timeout after the job started and any
other cancel in the attempt keeps it red. Like a cancelled attempt it is not conclusive: an earlier or newer conclusive
attempt of the run, or a conclusive run of the same commit, decides the commit instead. A commit left with only such an
attempt is treated like a flake ruling: the line reads "UNTESTED  run N on SHA: job J untested, no runner picked it up. Not a pass.",
and it exits 2 in plain mode and with --tip, 0 with --merge-gate. A red commit below it stays red. The jobs of a failed
run are read only for the commits the walk reaches.

Exit codes:
  0  green: the newest conclusive commit passed (it may be followed by untested commits while a run is going).
     With --tip: main's tip itself passed.
  1  red: the newest conclusive commit failed. Also any state it cannot read (gh or git error, bad journal, a run on
     a commit that is not on main's first-parent line).
  2  untested: main has commits no conclusive run tested and no run is going (start one), or there is no
     conclusive run at all, or a run left a job untested because no runner picked it up (above). The message says
     whether a run is going. With --tip, also a green commit below
     untested commits while a run is going: the tip is not tested yet, so wait.
Under --tip the GREEN line ends with the full 40-char tip sha ("tip <sha>"). A deploy pulls that sha
(git merge --ff-only <sha>), because main can move between the check and the pull.
Under --merge-gate, 2 becomes 0 (the line is unchanged), so the exit is 0 unless a repo is red or unreadable.
--all exits 1 if any repo is 1, else 2 if any repo is 2, else 0. homelab and amazon-itemizer have no main run: "n/a", never affects the code.

GitHub repos: the full workflow's runs on main, read from gh run list (the newest RUN_LIMIT runs).
coordinator: the coordinator journal, the last conclusive line for each tip (verdict pass, fail or flake) in
${XDG_STATE_HOME:-~/.local/state}/coordinator-ci/main-journeys.jsonl, and a run is going while the lock dir
/tmp/coordinator-main-journeys.lock.d holds a live pid. A line may carry "tree" (the tip's tree sha). A commit is
tested when a pass line has its tip, or a tree equal to the commit's tree (the walk uses this too); the GREEN line then
names the line and the tip that had the tree. Lines without "tree" match by tip only. A "flake" line (a red tip ruled
a flake, with "issue") is not red and not tested: plain mode and --tip both exit 2 for a flake with no later pass
(start a run), because a deploy needs a pass on the tip. A torn tail (what a crash leaves after the last complete line: NUL
bytes, a half line) is skipped with one stderr note that names the file and the byte count; a bad line before the last
complete line is still an unreadable journal (exit 1).
The first-parent walk reads one commit at a time (repos/R/commits/SHA, parents[0]). It stops at the first green,
or once every commit with a verdict has been reached. WALK_CAP is a backstop. Commit reads use gh's 1-hour cache (a commit
never changes); run list and branches/main are always read fresh.
Every gh call carries GH_CALLER=ci-main-status. --merge-gate and --tip also set GH_URGENT=1; plain and --all add nothing.
"""
import datetime
import itertools
import json
import os
import re
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import time
import traceback
import urllib.error
import urllib.request
from pathlib import Path
from urllib.parse import quote, urlparse

REPOS = {
    "dotfiles": {"github": "cartwmic/dotfiles", "workflow": "ci.yml"},
    "loop-engine": {"github": "cartwmic/loop-engine", "workflow": "ci.yml"},
    "agent-kit": {"github": "cartwmic/agent-kit", "workflow": "unit.yml"},
    "coordinator": {"github": "cartwmic/coordinator", "journal": True},
    "homelab": None,
    "amazon-itemizer": None,
    "alert-steward": {"github": "cartwmic/alert-steward", "workflow": "image.yml"},
    "storycraft": {"github": "StoryCraftTW/storycraft", "workflow": "ci.yml"},
    "retro": {"github": "cartwmic/retro", "workflow": "unit.yml"},
    "budget-steward": {"gitea": "cartwmic/budget-steward", "kgate": "budget-steward"},   # on the homelab Gitea: no CI runner; gated on Gitea status or a full-suite kgate run
    "eval-cases": {"github": "cartwmic/eval-cases", "no_ci": True},   # private, no CI, no required checks possible: gated on review verify + pr-body-check
}
# budget-steward is not in ORDER: --all must not fail on a machine that cannot reach Gitea (the work Mac, a pod with no token).
ORDER = ["dotfiles", "loop-engine", "agent-kit", "coordinator", "homelab", "amazon-itemizer", "alert-steward", "storycraft", "retro", "eval-cases"]
JOURNAL = Path(os.environ.get("CI_MAIN_STATUS_JOURNAL")
               or Path(os.environ.get("XDG_STATE_HOME") or Path.home() / ".local/state") / "coordinator-ci/main-journeys.jsonl")
LOCK = Path(os.environ.get("CI_MAIN_STATUS_LOCK") or "/tmp/coordinator-main-journeys.lock.d")
RUN_EVENTS = ("push", "workflow_dispatch")
RUN_FIELDS = "databaseId,attempt,event,headSha,status,conclusion,url"
RUN_LIMIT = 100
NO_RUNNER = "was not acquired by Runner"   # the annotation GitHub puts on a job it cancelled because no runner picked it up
UNPROVEN = ("flake", "untested")   # verdicts that are not red and not tested
JOURNAL_SPACE = b" \t\r\n"          # bytes that make a tail blank rather than torn
# The pin-fix exception. The step name and the file lists are copies: the step is in .github/workflows/ci.yml, the files are
# agent_kit_bump.py (KIT, PIN_FILES) and loop_engine_bump.py (MISE_CONFIG, SKILLS); tests/ci-main-status checks that they match.
PIN_FIX, RED_FIX = "the pin fix", "a fix"   # what --pr says it is not, in a refusal
PINS_STEP = "Release pins: fail when a Loop Engine or agent-kit pin lags the latest release"
AGENT_KIT_PIN_FILES = {"dot_local/share/agent-kit/package.json", "dot_local/share/agent-kit/package-lock.json"}
LOOP_ENGINE_MISE_CONFIG = "dot_config/mise/config.toml"
LOOP_ENGINE_SKILLS = "dot_local/share/agent-harness/canonical/skills/"
WALK_CAP = 250
CALLER = "ci-main-status"   # every gh call names its caller (GH_CALLER); the gh wrapper's log records it
URGENT = False              # set by main(): --merge-gate and --tip reads are urgent (GH_URGENT=1)


class Unreadable(Exception):
    """The state cannot be read: exit 1, never 0."""


class Record:
    def __init__(self, tip, verdict, label, rerun_going=False, tree=None, line=0, issue=None, run_id=None, attempt=None, unrun=()):
        self.tip, self.verdict, self.label = tip, verdict, label   # verdict: "pass", "fail", "untested" (GitHub) or (journal) "flake"
        self.unrun = list(unrun)   # "untested": the names of the jobs no runner picked up
        self.rerun_going = rerun_going   # the verdict is an earlier attempt, and a rerun of its run is going
        self.tree, self.line, self.issue = tree, line, issue   # journal only: the tip's tree, its line number, a flake's issue
        self.run_id, self.attempt = run_id, attempt   # GitHub only: the run and the attempt that gave the verdict

    def by_tree(self, sha):
        """This pass, read as the verdict of another commit `sha` with the same tree."""
        return Record(sha, "pass", f"{self.label} (tip {self.tip[:7]}, same tree)", tree=self.tree, line=self.line)


def gh(args, not_found_ok=False):
    """One gh call's JSON. not_found_ok: a 404 (GitHub answering there is nothing to read, such as an unprotected
    branch) gives None, for the caller to decide. Every other failure, a 403 included (no permission, a rate
    limit), still raises: fail closed."""
    env = {**os.environ, "GH_CALLER": CALLER}
    if URGENT:
        env["GH_URGENT"] = "1"
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(["gh", *args], capture_output=True, text=True, env=env)
    except OSError as e:
        raise Unreadable(f"gh could not start ({e.strerror}); is it on PATH?")
    if r.returncode:
        if not_found_ok and "HTTP 404" in r.stderr:
            return None
        raise Unreadable(f"gh {' '.join(args[:2])} failed: {r.stderr.strip() or r.stdout.strip()}")
    try:
        return json.loads(r.stdout)
    except json.JSONDecodeError as e:
        raise Unreadable(f"gh {' '.join(args[:2])} returned non-JSON: {e}")


def no_rulesets_on_plan(e):
    """True for exactly GitHub's refusal of a feature the repo's plan does not have: HTTP 403 with its "Upgrade to
    GitHub Pro or make this repository public" text. Any other 403 (a rate limit, no permission) is not this."""
    text = str(e)
    return "HTTP 403" in text and "Upgrade to GitHub Pro" in text


def main_tip(repo):
    return gh(["api", f"repos/{repo}/branches/main"])["commit"]["sha"]


CHECK_FREE_RULE_TYPES = frozenset({
    # The branch-rule types a merge can carry that cannot gate it on status checks, verified live as a non-admin
    # on public repos: branch-management rules, review rules, and the organization-level repository rules (they
    # govern repositories, not merges). required_status_checks is handled separately; every other type -- the
    # known CI gates (workflows, code_scanning, code_quality, required_deployments, code_coverage,
    # license_compliance_scanning) and anything GitHub adds later -- fails closed, so a new type can never
    # produce a wrong GREEN.
    "creation", "update", "deletion", "required_linear_history", "required_signatures", "non_fast_forward",
    "pull_request", "merge_queue", "copilot_code_review", "commit_message_pattern", "commit_author_email_pattern",
    "committer_email_pattern", "branch_name_pattern", "tag_name_pattern", "file_path_restriction",
    "max_file_path_length", "file_extension_restriction", "max_file_size", "repository_create", "repository_delete",
    "repository_name", "repository_transfer", "repository_visibility",
})


def required_checks(repo, branch, pr=None):
    """The exact set of status checks GitHub requires to merge into `branch` of `repo` -- or, with `pr`, into
    that PR's base (base.ref read from the pulls API). Unreadable whenever the full set cannot be known: never a
    smaller set, and never "none" unless proven. The decision table's rows:

    Both sources are always read; nothing returns before the rules are read. B = GET repos/{repo}/branches/{b}
    (row 1: any non-200, a 403 rate limit or a 404 included, is unreadable; read access is enough, and it carries
    protection.enabled and protection.required_status_checks to a non-admin -- the classic /protection endpoints
    answer 404 to a non-admin even when protection exists, so they are never called). R = GET
    repos/{repo}/rules/branches/{b}?per_page=100 --paginate (row 2: a non-200, or any page failing, is
    unreadable -- except GitHub's "Upgrade to GitHub Pro or make this repository public" 403, which a private
    repo on a free plan answers because it has no rulesets: that reads as no rules, and nothing else does), the active rules already merged across org and repo rulesets; the branch name is URL-encoded (a
    name with / must work). Row 3: a malformed response is unreadable -- an unexpected JSON value type at ANY
    depth the gate reads (an unknown rule TYPE is not malformed; row 5a handles it). Row 4: C is the classic set
    when protection.enabled, else empty; both checks[].context and contexts are read and de-duplicated, and an
    enabled protection whose required_status_checks is missing, or carries neither checks nor contexts, is
    unreadable -- no silent default. Row 5: S is the union of the rulesets' required_status_checks contexts.
    Row 5a: any rule type not known to be check-free is unreadable, never GREEN. Row 6: required = C | S.
    Rows 7-9: non-empty returns the set; empty and not protected returns the empty set (proven); empty and
    protected is unreadable -- nothing is required, so nothing could be proved.
    """
    if pr is not None:
        pull = gh(["api", f"repos/{repo}/pulls/{pr}"])   # non-200 -> unreadable
        if not isinstance(pull, dict) or not isinstance(pull.get("base"), dict) \
                or not isinstance(pull["base"].get("ref"), str):
            raise Unreadable(f"PR #{pr}: the pulls response has no base.ref; failing closed")
        branch = pull["base"]["ref"]

    def bad(what):
        return Unreadable(f"{branch}: {what}; failing closed")

    # Row 1: B non-200 raises. Rows 3-4: B's shape, then C.
    b = gh(["api", f"repos/{repo}/branches/{quote(branch, safe='')}"])
    if not isinstance(b, dict):
        raise bad("the branch response is not an object")
    protected = b.get("protected")
    if not isinstance(protected, bool):
        raise bad("the branch response's protected is not a bool")
    classic = set()
    if protected:
        protection = b.get("protection")
        if not isinstance(protection, dict):
            raise bad("the branch is protected but its protection is not an object")
        enabled = protection.get("enabled")
        if not isinstance(enabled, bool):
            raise bad("the branch is protected but protection.enabled is missing or not a bool")
        if enabled:
            rsc = protection.get("required_status_checks")
            if not isinstance(rsc, dict):
                raise bad("protection.enabled but required_status_checks is missing or not an object")
            checks, contexts = rsc.get("checks"), rsc.get("contexts")
            if checks is None and contexts is None:
                raise bad("protection.enabled with neither checks nor contexts in required_status_checks")
            if checks is not None:
                if not isinstance(checks, list):
                    raise bad("required_status_checks.checks is not a list")
                for c in checks:
                    if not isinstance(c, dict) or not isinstance(c.get("context"), str):
                        raise bad("a required_status_checks.checks item has no context string")
                    classic.add(c["context"])
            if contexts is not None:
                if not isinstance(contexts, list):
                    raise bad("required_status_checks.contexts is not a list")
                for c in contexts:
                    if not isinstance(c, str):
                        raise bad("a required_status_checks.contexts item is not a string")
                    classic.add(c)

    # Row 2: R non-200, or any page failing, raises. Row 3: R's shape. Rows 5 and 5a: S, and unknown types.
    try:
        rules = gh(["api", f"repos/{repo}/rules/branches/{quote(branch, safe='')}?per_page=100", "--paginate"])
    except Unreadable as e:
        if not no_rulesets_on_plan(e):
            raise
        rules = []   # a private repo on a free plan: GitHub says rulesets do not exist there, so none apply
    if not isinstance(rules, list):
        raise bad("the branch rules response is not an array")
    rulesets, unknown = set(), set()
    for r in rules:
        if not isinstance(r, dict):
            raise bad("a branch rules item is not an object")
        rtype = r.get("type")
        if not isinstance(rtype, str):
            raise bad("a branch rule's type is not a string")
        if rtype != "required_status_checks":
            if rtype not in CHECK_FREE_RULE_TYPES:
                unknown.add(rtype)   # row 5a, reported once every rule has been read
            continue
        params = r.get("parameters")
        if not isinstance(params, dict):
            raise bad("a required_status_checks rule has missing or invalid parameters")
        wanted = params.get("required_status_checks")
        if not isinstance(wanted, list):
            raise bad("a required_status_checks rule's parameters.required_status_checks is missing or not a list")
        for c in wanted:
            if not isinstance(c, dict) or not isinstance(c.get("context"), str):
                raise bad("a ruleset required_status_checks item has no context string")
            rulesets.add(c["context"])
    if unknown:   # row 5a: a type this gate cannot rule out is never GREEN
        raise Unreadable(f"{branch} also requires checks through rulesets of type {', '.join(sorted(unknown))}, "
                         f"which this gate cannot verify; check the PR's merge box by hand")

    # Rows 6-9.
    required = classic | rulesets
    if required:
        return required
    if not protected:
        return set()   # row 8: proven -- nothing is required
    raise Unreadable(f"{branch} is protected, but no required checks in protection or rulesets: "
                     f"nothing for this gate to verify")


def pr_rollup(repo, pr):
    """`gh pr checks --required` rows for PR `pr`, a cross-check on the computed required set only -- never the
    set the gate verifies (the rollup holds only checks present in the PR, so a required check that never started
    is missing from it). Exit 0 is the rollup; exit 1 (none reported) and exit 8 (some pending) leave the check
    to the computed set; any other exit is unreadable: fail closed."""
    env = {**os.environ, "GH_CALLER": CALLER}
    if URGENT:
        env["GH_URGENT"] = "1"
    args = ["pr", "checks", str(pr), "-R", repo, "--required", "--json", "name,state,bucket,link"]
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(["gh", *args], capture_output=True, text=True, env=env)
    except OSError as e:
        raise Unreadable(f"gh could not start ({e.strerror}); is it on PATH?")
    if r.returncode not in (0, 1, 8):
        raise Unreadable(f"gh pr checks --required failed (exit {r.returncode}): "
                         f"{r.stderr.strip() or r.stdout.strip()}")
    try:
        return json.loads(r.stdout) if r.stdout.strip() else []
    except json.JSONDecodeError as e:
        raise Unreadable(f"gh pr checks --required returned non-JSON: {e}")


def paged(repo, sha, what, field):
    """Every entry of a paged commit endpoint (check runs or statuses), read page by page at 100 a page.

    A page that comes back empty while the total count is not reached is an error, not a silent truncation (fail
    closed): gh --paginate cannot merge these endpoints' object pages, so the pages are asked for by number.
    """
    rows, page = [], 1
    sep = "&" if "?" in what else "?"
    while True:
        data = gh(["api", f"repos/{repo}/commits/{sha}/{what}{sep}per_page=100&page={page}"])
        rows += data[field]
        if len(rows) >= data["total_count"]:
            return rows
        if not data[field]:
            raise Unreadable(f"{what} page {page} on {sha[:7]} is empty but {data['total_count']} are counted")
        page += 1


WORSE = ("pass", "pending", "fail")   # worst of two verdicts for one required check wins


# The completed check-run conclusions GitHub's merge box accepts for a required status check.
PASSING_CONCLUSIONS = frozenset({"success", "skipped", "neutral"})


def check_verdicts(repo, sha, contexts):
    """{context: (verdict, detail)} for the required checks on `sha`: verdict "pass", "fail" or "pending", and the
    check run's conclusion or status (or the commit status's state) as the detail.

    Check runs (filter=latest, every page read): per name the newest run decides, the highest check-run id, which
    follows creation order — never a timestamp, which lets an older success hide a newer run still going, and never
    the last row the list happened to show. That run's status decides: queued or in_progress is pending (never a
    pass); a completed run passes when its conclusion is success, skipped or neutral, exactly the conclusions
    GitHub's merge box accepts for a required check (a job skipped by its `if:` reports skipped and does not block
    the merge); any other conclusion fails. A context no check run reports falls back to the commit's combined statuses (already the latest per
    context); when both report a name, the worse verdict wins, so a passing check run cannot hide a failing status.
    A name neither reports is pending (never a pass).
    """
    newest = {}
    for c in paged(repo, sha, "check-runs?filter=latest", "check_runs"):
        if c["name"] not in newest or c["id"] > newest[c["name"]]["id"]:   # the id is creation order: a newer
            newest[c["name"]] = c                                          # queued or running run is still newest
    verdicts, statuses = {}, None
    for name in contexts:
        c = newest.get(name)
        if c is None:
            verdicts[name] = None   # no check run: the commit status alone decides
        elif c["status"] == "completed" and c["conclusion"] in PASSING_CONCLUSIONS:
            verdicts[name] = ("pass", c["conclusion"])
        elif c["status"] != "completed":
            verdicts[name] = ("pending", c["status"])
        else:
            verdicts[name] = ("fail", c["conclusion"])
        if (verdicts[name] is None or verdicts[name][0] != "fail") and statuses is None:
            statuses = paged(repo, sha, "status", "statuses")   # a passing check run must not hide a failing status
    if statuses is None:   # every required check has a failed check run; nothing can make it worse
        return verdicts
    for name in contexts:
        s = next((s for s in statuses if s["context"] == name), None)
        sv = ({"success": "pass", "failure": "fail", "error": "fail"}.get(s["state"], "pending"), s["state"]) if s else None
        if verdicts[name] is None:
            verdicts[name] = sv or ("pending", "not reported")
        elif sv and WORSE.index(sv[0]) > WORSE.index(verdicts[name][0]):
            verdicts[name] = sv
    return verdicts


def check_any(repo, pr=None):
    """One GitHub repo not in the table: the required checks on its default branch's tip, or on PR `pr`'s head with --pr.

    The required set is the one required_checks computes for the branch (or, with --pr, for the PR's base), and
    that computed set is what the gate verifies on the tip or PR head -- never gh pr checks --required's list,
    which holds only checks present in the PR's rollup, so a required check that never started is missing from
    it and a name with no run on the head fails the gate. The rollup is a cross-check only: a name it marks
    required that the computed set lacks is an under-report, unreadable. When the required set cannot be computed
    (a read failing, a malformed response, an unknown rule type, nothing required), the state is unreadable:
    exit 1, never a pass.
    """
    if pr:
        pull = gh(["pr", "view", str(pr), "-R", repo, "--json", "headRefOid,baseRefName"])
        sha, base = pull["headRefOid"], pull["baseRefName"]
        where = f"PR #{pr} head {sha[:7]}"
        contexts = sorted(required_checks(repo, None, pr))
        extra = sorted({c["name"] for c in pr_rollup(repo, pr)} - set(contexts))
        if extra:
            raise Unreadable(f"GitHub's required checks for PR #{pr} include {', '.join(extra)}, which {base}'s "
                             f"computed required set does not; failing closed")
    else:
        branch = gh(["api", f"repos/{repo}"])["default_branch"]
        sha = gh(["api", f"repos/{repo}/branches/{quote(branch, safe='')}"])["commit"]["sha"]
        where = f"{branch} tip {sha[:7]}"
        contexts = sorted(required_checks(repo, branch))
    if not contexts:
        raise Unreadable(f"no required checks readable on {base if pr else branch} (branch protection or an active "
                         f"ruleset must require status checks, and the account must be allowed to read them); failing closed")
    verdicts = check_verdicts(repo, sha, contexts)
    failed = sorted(n for n, (v, _) in verdicts.items() if v == "fail")
    if failed:
        return 1, [f"{repo}: RED  required check(s) failed on {where}: {', '.join(failed)}"]
    pending = sorted(f"{n} ({d})" for n, (v, d) in verdicts.items() if v == "pending")
    if pending:
        return 2, [f"{repo}: UNTESTED  required check(s) pending on {where}: {', '.join(pending)}. Not a pass."]
    return 0, [f"{repo}: GREEN  all {len(contexts)} required checks passed on {where}: {', '.join(sorted(contexts))}"]


def describe_any(repo, pr=None):
    """Run one GitHub repo that is not in the table. A state it cannot read is one ERROR line and exit 1."""
    try:
        return check_any(repo, pr)
    except Unreadable as e:
        return 1, [f"{repo}: ERROR  cannot read state: {e}"]
    except Exception as e:   # a shape gh did not promise: one line on stdout, the traceback on stderr
        traceback.print_exc(file=sys.stderr)
        return 1, [f"{repo}: ERROR  cannot read state: unexpected {type(e).__name__}: {e}"]


def unrun_jobs(repo, run_id, attempt):
    """The names of the jobs a failed attempt never ran because no runner picked them up, or [] when it failed for any other reason.

    The attempt is untested only when every job in it that did not pass or skip was cancelled with GitHub's no-runner
    annotation. A failed job, a timeout, or a cancel with any other annotation keeps it a failure.
    """
    jobs = gh(["run", "view", str(run_id), "-R", repo, "--attempt", str(attempt), "--json", "jobs"])["jobs"]
    bad = not_ok(jobs)
    if not bad or any(j["conclusion"] != "cancelled" for j in bad):
        return []
    for j in bad:
        notes = gh(["api", f"repos/{repo}/check-runs/{j['databaseId']}/annotations"])
        if not any(NO_RUNNER in n["message"] for n in notes):
            return []
    return [j["name"] for j in bad]


def settle(repo, run_id, conclusion, attempt):
    """One concluded attempt as (verdict, attempt, unrun job names): its conclusion, or "untested" for a failure no runner caused."""
    unrun = unrun_jobs(repo, run_id, attempt) if conclusion == "failure" else []
    return ("untested", attempt, unrun) if unrun else (conclusion, attempt, [])


def concluded_attempts(repo, r):
    """The attempts of run `r` that concluded with success or failure, as (conclusion, attempt), newest first, read as asked.

    A rerun (gh run rerun) keeps the run id, so its newest attempt can be running or cancelled. Then the earlier
    attempts are read, one at a time, from the attempts API.
    """
    if r["status"] == "completed" and r["conclusion"] in ("success", "failure"):
        yield r["conclusion"], r["attempt"]
    for n in range(r["attempt"] - 1, 0, -1):
        conclusion = gh(["api", f"repos/{repo}/actions/runs/{r['databaseId']}/attempts/{n}"]).get("conclusion")
        if conclusion in ("success", "failure"):
            yield conclusion, n


def run_verdict(repo, r, attempts):
    """A run's verdict as (verdict, attempt, unrun job names). `attempts` is its concluded_attempts, at least one left.

    The newest attempt that concluded. An attempt left untested by a job no runner picked up is not conclusive,
    like a cancelled one: a conclusive attempt of the run wins, and without one the newest untested attempt is the verdict.
    """
    untested = None
    for conclusion, n in attempts:
        found = settle(repo, r["databaseId"], conclusion, n)
        if found[0] != "untested":
            return found
        untested = untested or found
    return untested


def run_record(r, found):
    verdict, attempt, unrun = found
    label = f"run {r['databaseId']}" + ("" if attempt == r["attempt"] else f" attempt {attempt}")
    return Record(r["headSha"], {"success": "pass", "failure": "fail", "untested": "untested"}[verdict], label,
                  rerun_going=r["status"] != "completed", run_id=r["databaseId"], attempt=attempt, unrun=unrun)


class CommitVerdicts:
    """{sha: Record} for the commits that have a run with a concluded attempt, read as the walk reaches them.

    A failed run's jobs (to tell a failure from a job no runner picked up) are fetched only for the commits the walk
    reaches, not for every failed run gh listed.
    """

    def __init__(self, repo, by_sha):
        self.repo = repo
        self.by_sha = by_sha   # {sha: [(run, its concluded_attempts with the first one peeked), ...]}, highest run id first
        self.records = {}      # {run id: Record}

    def __iter__(self):
        return iter(self.by_sha)

    def get(self, sha):
        return self[sha] if sha in self.by_sha else None

    def record(self, r, attempts):
        if r["databaseId"] not in self.records:
            self.records[r["databaseId"]] = run_record(r, run_verdict(self.repo, r, attempts))
        return self.records[r["databaseId"]]

    def __getitem__(self, sha):
        """One commit's verdict.

        The first run with a conclusive verdict counts, except that a red run whose rerun is going holds the commit red.
        A run left untested counts only when no run of the commit is conclusive.
        """
        runs = self.by_sha[sha]
        for r, attempts in runs:
            if r["status"] != "completed" and self.record(r, attempts).verdict == "fail":
                return self.records[r["databaseId"]]
        records = [self.record(r, attempts) for r, attempts in runs]
        return next((rec for rec in records if rec.verdict != "untested"), records[0])


def github_verdicts(spec):
    """The commit verdicts for the runs on main, as {sha: Record}, and whether a run is going."""
    runs = gh(["run", "list", "-R", spec["github"], "--workflow", spec["workflow"], "--branch", "main",
               "--limit", str(RUN_LIMIT), "--json", RUN_FIELDS])
    runs = [r for r in runs if r["event"] in RUN_EVENTS]
    going = any(r["status"] != "completed" for r in runs)
    by_sha = {}
    for r in sorted(runs, key=lambda r: r["databaseId"], reverse=True):   # run ids order runs of one commit
        attempts = concluded_attempts(spec["github"], r)
        first = next(attempts, None)   # a run with no concluded attempt gives its commit no verdict
        if first:
            by_sha.setdefault(r["headSha"], []).append((r, itertools.chain([first], attempts)))
    return CommitVerdicts(spec["github"], by_sha), going


def is_complete(raw):
    """True when `raw` (one journal line, no newline) is a JSON object. Read as bytes, so a torn line cannot fail the decode."""
    try:
        return isinstance(json.loads(raw.decode("utf-8")), dict)
    except (UnicodeDecodeError, ValueError):
        return False


def complete_end(data):
    """The offset just past the journal's last complete line and its newline, or 0 when there is none. What follows it is the
    torn tail. A complete last line with no newline counts as complete."""
    keep = start = 0
    for raw in data.split(b"\n"):
        end = min(start + len(raw) + 1, len(data))
        if is_complete(raw):
            keep = end
        start = end
    return keep


def journal_verdicts():
    """The last conclusive journal line for each tip, as {tip: Record}, and whether a live lock says a run is going.

    Conclusive means pass, fail or flake. A line may carry "tree" (the tip's tree sha); a tip whose last line is a
    pass also tests every commit with that tree. A flake line ({"tip","tree","verdict":"flake","issue","ruled"}) is a
    red tip ruled a flake: not red, and not tested. The torn tail after the last complete line is skipped, with a note on
    stderr; a file with no complete line has no verdict.
    """
    verdicts = {}
    if JOURNAL.exists():
        data = JOURNAL.read_bytes()
        keep = complete_end(data)
        if data[keep:].strip(JOURNAL_SPACE):
            print(f"ci-main-status: skipped a torn tail of {len(data) - keep} bytes in {JOURNAL}; "
                  + ("using the last complete line" if keep else "no complete line is left"), file=sys.stderr)
        for n, line in enumerate(data[:keep].decode("utf-8").split("\n"), 1):
            if not line.strip():
                continue
            try:
                row = json.loads(line)
            except json.JSONDecodeError as e:
                raise Unreadable(f"{JOURNAL} line {n} is not JSON: {e}")
            if not isinstance(row, dict):
                raise Unreadable(f"{JOURNAL} line {n} is not a JSON object")
            if row.get("verdict") in ("pass", "fail", "flake"):
                if not row.get("tip"):
                    raise Unreadable(f"{JOURNAL} line {n} has a {row['verdict']} verdict and no tip")
                tree = row.get("tree")
                if tree is not None and not isinstance(tree, str):
                    raise Unreadable(f"{JOURNAL} line {n} has a tree that is not a string")
                verdicts[row["tip"]] = Record(row["tip"], row["verdict"], f"journal line {n}", tree=tree or None,
                                              line=n, issue=row.get("issue"))   # the last line wins
    return verdicts, lock_alive()


def passing_trees(verdicts):
    """{tree: Record} for the tips whose last line is a pass with a tree. The newest line wins."""
    trees = {}
    for rec in sorted(verdicts.values(), key=lambda r: r.line):
        if rec.verdict == "pass" and rec.tree:
            trees[rec.tree] = rec
    return trees


def verdict_of(sha, tree, verdicts, trees):
    """A commit's verdict: its own pass; else a same-tree pass that comes after its own line (or any, if it has none);
    else its own fail or flake line; else None.

    An older same-tree pass never overrides the commit's own newer fail or flake, so a ruling cannot make the tip tested.
    """
    own = verdicts.get(sha)
    if own and own.verdict == "pass":
        return own
    same_tree = trees.get(tree)
    if same_tree and (own is None or same_tree.line > own.line):
        return same_tree.by_tree(sha)
    return own


def lock_alive():
    try:
        pid = int((LOCK / "pid").read_text().strip())
        os.kill(pid, 0)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return False
    return True


def first_parent_walk(repo, tip, verdicts, trees=None):
    """Main's first-parent commits from the tip, newest first, as (sha, subject, Record or None).

    The walk stops at the first pass, or once every commit with a verdict has been reached. If it runs out first
    (the root, or WALK_CAP) with a verdict's commit still unreached, that commit is not on main's first-parent
    history as far as the walk can see, and the state is unreadable. trees ({tree: pass Record}, journal only) lets a
    commit take the pass of another tip with the same tree.
    """
    trees = trees or {}
    walked, pending, cur = [], set(verdicts), tip
    while pending and cur and len(walked) < WALK_CAP:
        c = gh(["api", f"repos/{repo}/commits/{cur}", "--cache", "1h"])   # a commit never changes, so the 1-hour cache is exact
        rec = verdict_of(cur, c["commit"].get("tree", {}).get("sha"), verdicts, trees)
        walked.append((cur, c["commit"]["message"].split("\n")[0], rec))
        pending.discard(cur)
        if rec and rec.verdict == "pass":
            return walked
        parents = c.get("parents") or []
        cur = parents[0]["sha"] if parents else None
    if pending:
        missing = sorted(pending)[0]
        raise Unreadable(f"{verdicts[missing].label} on {missing[:7]} is not on the first-parent history of main "
                         f"(not reached in {len(walked)} commit(s) walked from {tip[:7]}, or beyond the cap of {WALK_CAP})")
    return walked


def pin_files_only(names):
    """True when `names` (a PR's changed files) are only bump pin files: agent-kit's two, the Loop Engine mise config plus skills, or both (one combined bump PR)."""
    names = set(names)
    kit, rest = names & AGENT_KIT_PIN_FILES, names - AGENT_KIT_PIN_FILES
    if not names or (kit and kit != AGENT_KIT_PIN_FILES):
        return False
    return not rest or (LOOP_ENGINE_MISE_CONFIG in rest and all(n == LOOP_ENGINE_MISE_CONFIG or n.startswith(LOOP_ENGINE_SKILLS) for n in rest))


def not_ok(steps):
    """The steps (or jobs) that neither passed nor were skipped."""
    return [s for s in steps if s["conclusion"] not in ("success", "skipped")]


def only_pins_step_failed(jobs):
    """Exactly one job failed, and the release-pins step is the only step in it that did not pass or skip."""
    bad_jobs = not_ok(jobs)
    if len(bad_jobs) != 1 or bad_jobs[0]["conclusion"] != "failure":
        return False
    bad_steps = not_ok(bad_jobs[0]["steps"])
    return len(bad_steps) == 1 and bad_steps[0]["conclusion"] == "failure" and bad_steps[0]["name"].startswith(PINS_STEP)


def pin_fix_reason(spec, red, pr):
    """Why PR `pr` may merge into a red dotfiles main as the pin fix, or None. Prints the reason it may not to stderr. A gh failure is a refusal, not an error."""
    repo = spec["github"]
    try:
        jobs = gh(["run", "view", str(red.run_id), "-R", repo, "--attempt", str(red.attempt), "--json", "jobs"])["jobs"]
        if not only_pins_step_failed(jobs):
            return refuse(pr, f"{red.label} failed on more than the release-pins step", PIN_FIX)
        pull = gh(["pr", "view", str(pr), "-R", repo, "--json", "files,headRefOid,changedFiles"])
        names = [f["path"] for f in pull["files"]]
        if pull["changedFiles"] != len(names):   # gh lists a PR's files in pages and may return only the first
            return refuse(pr, f"gh listed {len(names)} of its {pull['changedFiles']} changed files", PIN_FIX)
        if not pin_files_only(names):
            return refuse(pr, f"its diff is not exactly the pin files: {', '.join(names) or 'nothing'}", PIN_FIX)
        head = pull["headRefOid"]
        own = [r for r in gh(["run", "list", "-R", repo, "--workflow", spec["workflow"], "--commit", head, "--event", "pull_request",
                              "--limit", "20", "--json", "databaseId,headSha,status,conclusion"]) if r["headSha"] == head]
        if not own:
            return refuse(pr, f"no pull_request run of {head[:7]}", PIN_FIX)
        newest = max(own, key=lambda r: r["databaseId"])   # run ids order runs of one commit
        if newest["status"] != "completed" or newest["conclusion"] != "success":
            return refuse(pr, f"its own run {newest['databaseId']} is {newest['conclusion'] or newest['status']}, not success", PIN_FIX)
        own_jobs = gh(["run", "view", str(newest["databaseId"]), "-R", repo, "--json", "jobs"])["jobs"]
        steps = [s for j in own_jobs for s in j["steps"] if s["name"].startswith(PINS_STEP)]
        if len(steps) != 1 or steps[0]["conclusion"] != "success":
            return refuse(pr, f"its own run {newest['databaseId']} did not pass the release-pins step", PIN_FIX)
        return (f"  merge-gate: PR #{pr} is the pin fix for this red: only the release-pins step failed, the PR changes only the pin files, "
                f"and its own run {newest['databaseId']} passed that step. Allowed.")
    except (Unreadable, KeyError, TypeError) as e:
        return refuse(pr, f"could not read it ({e})", PIN_FIX)


def refuse(pr, why, kind=RED_FIX):
    print(f"ci-main-status: --pr {pr} is not {kind} for this red: {why}", file=sys.stderr)
    return None


def red_jobs(repo, red):
    """The jobs of main's red attempt that did not pass or skip, as {job name: names of its steps that did not pass or skip}."""
    jobs = gh(["run", "view", str(red.run_id), "-R", repo, "--attempt", str(red.attempt), "--json", "jobs"])["jobs"]
    return {j["name"]: [s["name"] for s in not_ok(j["steps"])] for j in not_ok(jobs)}


def judge_run(repo, run, wanted):
    """How one run on the PR's tree answers main's red: ("skipped", why), ("bad", why) or ("good", None).

    skipped: the run did not run a job or step that failed in main (a pull_request run that skips the full suite), so it says nothing.
    bad: it ran them and they did not all pass, or it did not succeed, or it is still going with its red jobs and steps listed.
    A run still going whose red job has no steps listed yet (queued, nothing started) is read as skipped: it has run nothing, so it
    says nothing, and the next older run on the same tree decides. It does not refuse. Once its steps are listed it is "bad".
    """
    jobs = {j["name"]: j for j in gh(["run", "view", str(run["databaseId"]), "-R", repo, "--json", "jobs"])["jobs"]}
    for name, step_names in wanted.items():
        job = jobs.get(name)
        if job is None or job["conclusion"] == "skipped":
            return "skipped", f"run {run['databaseId']} skipped job {name}"
        steps = {s["name"]: s for s in job["steps"]}
        for step in step_names:
            if step not in steps or steps[step]["conclusion"] == "skipped":
                return "skipped", f"run {run['databaseId']} skipped step \"{step}\" in job {name}"
    if run["status"] != "completed":
        return "bad", f"run {run['databaseId']} is {run['status']}, not success"
    for name, step_names in wanted.items():
        if jobs[name]["conclusion"] != "success" or any(s["conclusion"] != "success" for s in jobs[name]["steps"] if s["name"] in step_names):
            return "bad", f"run {run['databaseId']} did not pass {name}"
    if run["conclusion"] != "success":
        return "bad", f"run {run['databaseId']} is {run['conclusion']}, not success"
    return "good", None


def red_fix_reason(spec, red, pr):
    """Why PR `pr` may merge into a red main, or None: its own full-suite run on its head tree passed what failed in main.

    The runs are those of the same workflow on the PR's head commit or on a commit with its tree, newest first. One that skipped a
    job or step that failed in main is passed over; the first one that ran them all decides. Prints why not to stderr. A gh failure
    is a refusal, not an error.
    """
    repo = spec["github"]
    try:
        wanted = red_jobs(repo, red)
        pull = gh(["pr", "view", str(pr), "-R", repo, "--json", "headRefOid,headRefName"])
        head = pull["headRefOid"]
        tree = tree_of(repo, head)
        listing = ["run", "list", "-R", repo, "--workflow", spec["workflow"], "--limit", "100", "--json", RUN_FIELDS]
        runs = {r["databaseId"]: r for r in gh(listing + ["--commit", head]) + gh(listing + ["--branch", pull["headRefName"]])}
        passed_over = []
        for run in sorted(runs.values(), key=lambda r: r["databaseId"], reverse=True):   # run ids order runs of one workflow
            if run["headSha"] != head and tree_of(repo, run["headSha"]) != tree:
                continue
            verdict, why = judge_run(repo, run, wanted)
            if verdict == "bad":
                return refuse(pr, why)
            if verdict == "good":
                same = "" if run["headSha"] == head else f", same tree as its head {head[:7]}"
                return (f"  merge-gate: PR #{pr} passed as a red-main fix: its own full-suite run {run['databaseId']} ({run['url']}) "
                        f"on {run['headSha'][:7]}{same} succeeded, and ran and passed every job and step that failed in {red.label} "
                        f"({', '.join(wanted)}). Allowed.")
            passed_over.append(why)
        return refuse(pr, "no full-suite run of its head tree" + (": " + "; ".join(passed_over) if passed_over
                                                                     else f": no {spec['workflow']} run of {head[:7]} or of a commit with its tree"))
    except (Unreadable, KeyError, TypeError) as e:
        return refuse(pr, f"could not read it ({e})")


def tree_of(repo, sha):
    return gh(["api", f"repos/{repo}/commits/{sha}"])["commit"]["tree"]["sha"]


def fix_reason(name, spec, red, pr):
    """The "merge-gate:" line for PR `pr` as the fix for a red main, or None (the refusal went to stderr)."""
    if red.run_id is None:
        return refuse(pr, "the red verdict is not a GitHub run")
    if name == "dotfiles":   # the pin rule first (its own checks), then the rule every other repo gets
        return pin_fix_reason(spec, red, pr) or red_fix_reason(spec, red, pr)
    return red_fix_reason(spec, red, pr)


def untested_line(name, sha, rec):
    """The UNTESTED line for a commit whose run left jobs untested because no runner picked them up."""
    one = len(rec.unrun) == 1
    return (f"{name}: UNTESTED  {rec.label} on {sha[:7]}: {'job' if one else 'jobs'} {', '.join(rec.unrun)} untested, "
            f"no runner picked {'it' if one else 'them'} up. Not a pass.")


def assess(name, repo, verdicts, going, noun="run", tip_only=False, trees=None, spec=None, pr=None):
    """One repo's state. Returns (exit code, output lines). Used by every repo kind.

    tip_only (--tip): green below untested commits is 2 even while a run is going.
    """
    tip = main_tip(repo)
    walked = first_parent_walk(repo, tip, verdicts, trees)
    hits = [i for i, (_, _, rec) in enumerate(walked) if rec and rec.verdict not in UNPROVEN]
    unproven = [w for w in walked[:hits[0] if hits else len(walked)] if w[2] and w[2].verdict in UNPROVEN]
    if unproven and not (hits and walked[hits[0]][2].verdict == "fail"):
        # A flake ruling, or a job no runner picked up, is not red and not tested (ask #854: a deploy needs a pass on the tip).
        sha, _, rec = unproven[0]
        if rec.verdict == "untested":
            lines = [untested_line(name, sha, rec)]
        else:
            issue = f" (issue {rec.issue})" if rec.issue else ""
            lines = [f"{name}: UNTESTED  {rec.label} ruled {sha[:7]} a flake{issue}; a flake is not a pass."]
        lines.append("  A run is going; wait for it." if going else "  No run is going. Start a run.")
        return 2, lines
    if not hits:
        where = f"no conclusive {noun} on main; main tip {tip[:7]}"
        if going:
            return 2, [f"{name}: UNTESTED  {where}. A run is going; wait for it."]
        return 2, [f"{name}: UNTESTED  {where}, and no run is going. Start one."]

    i = hits[0]
    sha, _, newest = walked[i]
    if newest.verdict == "fail":
        note = "  (a rerun is going)" if newest.rerun_going else ("  (a newer run is going)" if going else "")
        lines = [f"{name}: RED  {newest.label} failed on {sha[:7]}{note}"]

        def red():
            allowed = fix_reason(name, spec, newest, pr) if pr is not None else None
            return (0, lines + [allowed]) if allowed else (1, lines)

        greens = [j for j in hits if walked[j][2].verdict == "pass"]
        if not greens:
            lines.append("  no earlier green run; red range not computed")
            return red()
        j = greens[0]
        green_sha, _, green = walked[j]
        lines.append(f"  last green: {green_sha[:7]} ({green.label})")
        lines.append("  first-parent commits last green..red tip:")
        lines += [f"    {s[:7]} {subject}" for s, subject, _ in walked[i:j]]
        return red()

    untested = i
    if untested == 0:
        full = f"; tip {sha}" if tip_only else ""
        return 0, [f"{name}: GREEN  {newest.label} passed on {sha[:7]}; main tip is tested{full}"]
    if going and tip_only:
        return 2, [f"{name}: UNTESTED  {untested} main commit(s) after {newest.label} ({sha[:7]}); "
                   f"main tip {tip[:7]} is not tested yet. A run is going; wait for it."]
    if going:
        return 0, [f"{name}: GREEN  {newest.label} passed on {sha[:7]}; "
                   f"{untested} main commit(s) not tested yet, a run is going"]
    return 2, [f"{name}: UNTESTED  {untested} main commit(s) after {newest.label} ({sha[:7]}) "
               f"and no run is going. Start one."]


def run_step(label, argv):
    """One gate step's (ok, one line saying what it said). A program that cannot start, or exits non-zero, is not ok."""
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(argv, capture_output=True, text=True)
    except OSError as e:
        return False, f"{label}: FAILED  {argv[0]} could not start ({e.strerror}); is it on PATH?"
    said = [line.strip() for line in (r.stdout + r.stderr).splitlines() if line.strip()]
    if r.returncode:
        return False, f"{label}: FAILED  exit {r.returncode}: {said[-1] if said else 'no output'}"
    first = said[0].removeprefix(label + ": ") if said else "no output"
    return True, f"{label}: OK  {first}"


def no_ci_gate(name, spec, pr):
    """The merge gate of a repo with no CI: PR `pr`'s review verify at its head and its body check, both run, both must exit 0."""
    repo = spec["github"]
    head = gh(["pr", "view", str(pr), "-R", repo, "--json", "headRefOid"])["headRefOid"]
    steps = [run_step("review verify", ["agent-traces", "review", "verify", "--item", f"{name}#{pr}", "--head", head, "--require-block"]),
             run_step("pr-body-check", ["pr-body-check", repo, str(pr)])]
    where = f"{repo} PR #{pr} head {head}"
    if all(ok for ok, _ in steps):
        return 0, [f"{name}: no CI (no required checks are possible on this repo). Passed on review verify and pr-body-check for {where}"] + [f"    {line}" for _, line in steps]
    return 1, [f"{name}: RED  no CI, and the merge gate failed for {where}"] + [f"    {line}" for _, line in steps]


def no_ci(name, spec, tip_only, pr, gate):
    if gate and pr:
        return no_ci_gate(name, spec, pr)
    if gate:
        return 1, [f"{name}: ERROR  no CI, so the merge gate is the PR's review verify and body check, and it cannot tell which PR is merging. "
                   f"Pass --pr N: ci-main-status --merge-gate {name} --pr N"]
    return 0, [f"{name}: n/a (no CI, no required checks possible; its merge gate is ci-main-status --merge-gate {name} --pr N)"]


# ---- Gitea repos (budget-steward): no gh, no CI runner. See the docstring.
GITEA_API_DEFAULT = "https://gitea.internal.cartwmic.com/api/v1"
GITEA_SUITE = ("npm run typecheck", "npm test")   # a kgate command that ran the whole unit gate holds both
SHA40 = re.compile(r"^[0-9a-f]{40}$")


def gitea_api():
    return (os.environ.get("CI_MAIN_STATUS_GITEA_API") or GITEA_API_DEFAULT).rstrip("/")


_TOKEN = []   # the token, fetched once per run: a credential helper that prompts must prompt once, not once per Gitea read


def gitea_token():
    """The Gitea token: CI_MAIN_STATUS_GITEA_TOKEN, else the git credential for the Gitea host. None when there is none. Never printed.
    Fetched once per run."""
    if not _TOKEN:
        _TOKEN.append(fetch_gitea_token())
    return _TOKEN[0]


def fetch_gitea_token():
    token = os.environ.get("CI_MAIN_STATUS_GITEA_TOKEN")
    if token:
        return token
    url = urlparse(gitea_api())
    if not url.hostname:
        return None
    ask = f"protocol={url.scheme}\nhost={url.netloc}\n\n"
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(["git", "credential", "fill"], input=ask, capture_output=True, text=True,
                           env={**os.environ, "GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT": "0"}, timeout=20)
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        return None
    for line in r.stdout.splitlines():
        if line.startswith("password="):
            return line[len("password="):] or None
    return None


def gitea_get(path):
    """One Gitea API read as JSON. Any failure (no token for a private repo included: Gitea answers 404) raises Unreadable."""
    token = gitea_token()
    request = urllib.request.Request(gitea_api() + path, headers={"Authorization": "token " + token} if token else {})
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(request, timeout=30) as response:
            return json.loads(response.read().decode())
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:
        hint = "" if token else " (no Gitea token: set CI_MAIN_STATUS_GITEA_TOKEN or a git credential for the Gitea host; a private repo answers 404 without one)"
        raise Unreadable(f"Gitea GET {path}: HTTP {e.code}{hint}")
    except (urllib.error.URLError, OSError, ValueError) as e:
        raise Unreadable(f"Gitea GET {path} failed: {e}")


def kgate_log_path():
    return Path(os.environ.get("CI_MAIN_STATUS_KGATE_LOG")
                or Path(os.environ.get("XDG_STATE_HOME") or Path.home() / ".local/state") / "kgate/log.jsonl")


def kgate_verdict(name, tree):
    """The newest full-suite kgate run of repo `name` on git tree `tree`, as ("pass" | "fail", job id), or None."""
    try:
        lines = kgate_log_path().read_text(errors="replace").splitlines()
    except OSError:
        return None   # no log: no evidence
    found = None
    for line in lines:
        try:
            r = json.loads(line)
        except ValueError:
            continue   # a torn or foreign line is not a record
        if not isinstance(r, dict) or r.get("repo") != name or r.get("tree") != tree or r.get("ran") is not True or r.get("cancelled"):
            continue
        cmd = r.get("cmd")
        if not isinstance(cmd, str) or not all(w in cmd for w in GITEA_SUITE):
            continue
        code = r.get("exit")
        if isinstance(code, int) and not isinstance(code, bool):
            found = ("pass" if code == 0 else "fail", str(r.get("id")))   # file order is time order: the newest run decides
    return found


def gitea_tree(repo, sha):
    """The git tree hash of commit `sha`, from a one-commit fetch of it. Gitea's API cannot say it: git/commits/SHA and git/trees/SHA
    both put the commit's own sha where the tree's belongs. kgate hashes the shipped files as `git write-tree` does, so this is the
    hash a kgate record carries. The token goes in git's environment, never argv."""
    url = os.environ.get("CI_MAIN_STATUS_GITEA_GIT") or f"{gitea_api().removesuffix('/api/v1')}/{repo}.git"
    token = gitea_token()
    env = {**os.environ, "GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT": "0"}
    if token:
        env.update(GIT_CONFIG_COUNT="1", GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0="http.extraHeader", GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0="Authorization: token " + token)
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="ci-main-status-") as work:
        try:
            for argv in (["init", "-q"], ["fetch", "-q", "--depth", "1", "--no-tags", url, sha], ["rev-parse", "FETCH_HEAD^{tree}"]):
                r = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", work, *argv], capture_output=True, text=True, env=env, timeout=120)
                if r.returncode:
                    raise Unreadable(f"git {argv[0]} of {repo} {sha[:7]} failed: {r.stderr.strip().replace(token or chr(0), '<token>')[:200]}")
        except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as e:
            raise Unreadable(f"git could not read {repo} {sha[:7]}: {e}")
    tree = r.stdout.strip()
    if not SHA40.match(tree):
        raise Unreadable(f"git gave no tree hash for {repo} {sha[:7]}; failing closed")
    return tree


def gitea_evidence(name, spec, sha, rec):
    """(verdict, what it rests on) for commit `sha`: "pass", "fail" or None (no evidence). The worse source wins. `rec` is the
    run's log record: the sha, the tree and the evidence read go into it as they are found, so an error halfway still logs what it had."""
    repo = spec["gitea"]
    rec["sha"] = sha
    tree = rec["tree"] = gitea_tree(repo, sha)
    status = gitea_get(f"/repos/{repo}/commits/{sha}/status")
    if not isinstance(status, dict) or not isinstance(status.get("total_count"), int):
        raise Unreadable(f"Gitea commit status of {sha[:7]} is malformed; failing closed")
    found = []   # (verdict, label)
    rec["evidence"] = {"gitea_status": status.get("state") if status["total_count"] > 0 else None, "kgate_job": None}
    if status["total_count"] > 0 and status.get("state") == "success":
        found.append(("pass", "Gitea commit status success"))
    elif status["total_count"] > 0 and status.get("state") in ("failure", "error"):
        found.append(("fail", f"Gitea commit status {status['state']}"))
    kg = kgate_verdict(spec["kgate"], tree)
    if kg:
        rec["evidence"]["kgate_job"] = kg[1]
        found.append((kg[0], f"kgate {kg[1]} exit {'0' if kg[0] == 'pass' else 'not 0'} on tree {tree[:7]}"))
    for verdict in ("fail", "pass"):
        hit = [label for v, label in found if v == verdict]
        if hit:
            return verdict, "; ".join(hit)
    return None, ""


def gitea_pr_gate(name, spec, pr, rec):
    repo = spec["gitea"]
    pull = gitea_get(f"/repos/{repo}/pulls/{pr}")
    head = pull.get("head", {}).get("sha") if isinstance(pull, dict) and isinstance(pull.get("head"), dict) else None
    base = pull.get("base", {}).get("ref") if isinstance(pull, dict) and isinstance(pull.get("base"), dict) else None
    if not isinstance(head, str) or not SHA40.match(head) or not isinstance(base, str):
        raise Unreadable(f"Gitea PR #{pr} has no readable head and base; failing closed")
    rec["sha"] = head
    where = f"{repo} PR #{pr} head {head[:7]}"
    if pull.get("state") != "open":
        return 1, [f"{name}: RED  {where} is not open (state {pull.get('state')!r})"]
    if base != "main":
        return 1, [f"{name}: RED  {where} is aimed at {base}, not main"]
    verdict, what = gitea_evidence(name, spec, head, rec)
    if verdict == "pass":
        code, lines = check_threads(repo, pr)   # this repo's only merge gate: the unresolved-thread check has no other place to run
        if code:   # the verdict line comes first, because log_gitea reads the verdict from it: a thread refusal is RED (or ERROR), never GREEN
            kind = "ERROR" if ": ERROR " in lines[0] else "RED"
            return code, [f"{name}: {kind}  {where}: the evidence passed ({what}), but the review threads refuse it"] + lines
        return 0, [f"{name}: GREEN  {where}: {what}"] + lines
    if verdict == "fail":
        return 1, [f"{name}: RED  {where}: {what}"]
    return 1, [f"{name}: RED  {where}: no evidence. It needs a Gitea commit status success or a kgate run that ran `npm run typecheck` and `npm test` "
                f"on this exact tree and exited 0 (run `kgate -- sh -c 'npm ci && npm run typecheck && npm test'` in the PR's checkout)."]


def gitea_check(name, spec, tip_only, pr, gate, rec):
    if gate:
        if not pr:
            return 1, [f"{name}: ERROR  its merge gate is a PR's kgate or Gitea status evidence, and it cannot tell which PR is merging. "
                       f"Pass --pr N: ci-main-status --merge-gate {name} --pr N"]
        return gitea_pr_gate(name, spec, pr, rec)
    branch = gitea_get(f"/repos/{spec['gitea']}/branches/main")
    tip = branch.get("commit", {}).get("id") if isinstance(branch, dict) and isinstance(branch.get("commit"), dict) else None
    if not isinstance(tip, str) or not SHA40.match(tip):
        raise Unreadable("Gitea branches/main has no readable commit id; failing closed")
    verdict, what = gitea_evidence(name, spec, tip, rec)
    if verdict == "pass":
        return 0, [f"{name}: GREEN  {what} on {tip[:7]}; main tip is tested" + (f"; tip {tip}" if tip_only else "")]
    if verdict == "fail":
        return 1, [f"{name}: RED  {what} on {tip[:7]}"]
    return 2, [f"{name}: UNTESTED  no Gitea commit status and no full-suite kgate run on main {tip[:7]}'s tree. "
               f"Its merge gate is ci-main-status --merge-gate {name} --pr N."]


THREADS_QUERY = """query($owner: String!, $name: String!, $pr: Int!, $after: String) {
  repository(owner: $owner, name: $name) { pullRequest(number: $pr) {
    reviewThreads(first: 100, after: $after) {
      pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor }
      nodes { isResolved path line originalLine comments(first: 1) { nodes { body url } } } } } } }"""
THREAD_LIMIT = 50   # Gitea reads: page size
THREAD_PAGES = 40   # a backstop: 2000 reviews or comments on one PR is a read gone wrong


def first_line(text):
    """The first non-empty line of a comment, cut to 120 characters."""
    for line in str(text or "").splitlines():
        if line.strip():
            return line.strip()[:120]
    return ""


def thread(path, line, text, url):
    place = path or "(no file)"
    return {"where": f"{place}:{line}" if line else place, "text": first_line(text), "url": url or ""}


def github_threads(repo, pr):
    """The unresolved review threads of GitHub PR `pr`, outdated ones included. Paged by hand: gh's --paginate prints one JSON document per page."""
    owner, name = repo.split("/", 1)
    found, after = [], None
    for _ in range(THREAD_PAGES):
        args = ["api", "graphql", "-f", "query=" + THREADS_QUERY, "-f", "owner=" + owner, "-f", "name=" + name, "-F", f"pr={pr}"]
        if after:
            args += ["-f", "after=" + after]
        data = gh(args)
        if not isinstance(data, dict) or data.get("errors"):
            raise Unreadable(f"GitHub's review threads of {repo}#{pr} came back with errors: {json.dumps(data.get('errors') if isinstance(data, dict) else data)[:300]}")
        try:
            pull = data["data"]["repository"]["pullRequest"]
            threads = pull["reviewThreads"]
            nodes, more = threads["nodes"], threads["pageInfo"]
        except (KeyError, TypeError):
            raise Unreadable(f"GitHub has no readable review threads for {repo}#{pr} (no such PR, or a shape this check does not know); failing closed")
        for t in nodes:
            if not isinstance(t, dict) or not isinstance(t.get("isResolved"), bool):
                raise Unreadable(f"a review thread of {repo}#{pr} is malformed; failing closed")
            if t["isResolved"]:
                continue
            comments = (t.get("comments") or {}).get("nodes") or [{}]
            found.append(thread(t.get("path"), t.get("line") or t.get("originalLine"), comments[0].get("body"), comments[0].get("url")))
        if not more.get("hasNextPage"):
            return found
        after = more.get("endCursor")
        if not after:
            raise Unreadable(f"GitHub says there are more review threads of {repo}#{pr} but gave no cursor; failing closed")
    raise Unreadable(f"more than {THREAD_PAGES} pages of review threads on {repo}#{pr}; failing closed")


def gitea_paged(path):
    """Every item of a Gitea list endpoint, page by page."""
    items = []
    for page in range(1, THREAD_PAGES + 1):
        got = gitea_get(f"{path}{'&' if '?' in path else '?'}limit={THREAD_LIMIT}&page={page}")
        if not isinstance(got, list):
            raise Unreadable(f"Gitea GET {path} did not return a list; failing closed")
        items += got
        if len(got) < THREAD_LIMIT:
            return items
    raise Unreadable(f"more than {THREAD_PAGES} pages from Gitea GET {path}; failing closed")


def gitea_threads(repo, pr):
    """The unresolved conversations of Gitea PR `pr`, every one that is not resolved."""
    groups = {}   # (path, original diff position) -> [the conversation's first comment, resolved?]
    for review in gitea_paged(f"/repos/{repo}/pulls/{pr}/reviews"):
        if not isinstance(review, dict) or not isinstance(review.get("id"), int):
            raise Unreadable(f"a Gitea review of {repo}#{pr} is malformed; failing closed")
        if review.get("state") == "PENDING":
            continue   # a draft its author has not submitted
        comments = gitea_get(f"/repos/{repo}/pulls/{pr}/reviews/{review['id']}/comments")   # no page or limit parameter (the 1.26 swagger): all of the review's comments come at once
        if not isinstance(comments, list):
            raise Unreadable(f"Gitea review {review['id']} of {repo}#{pr} did not return a list of comments; failing closed")
        for c in comments:
            if not isinstance(c, dict) or "resolver" not in c:
                raise Unreadable(f"a Gitea review comment of {repo}#{pr} has no `resolver` field (an older Gitea?); failing closed")
            key = (c.get("path"), c.get("original_position"))
            group = groups.setdefault(key, [c, False])
            group[1] = group[1] or c["resolver"] is not None
    return [thread(c.get("path"), None, c.get("body"), c.get("html_url")) for c, resolved in groups.values() if not resolved]


def thread_repo(arg):
    """(OWNER/REPO, on Gitea?) for a table name, OWNER/REPO, or a bare name taken as cartwmic/NAME."""
    spec = REPOS.get(arg)
    slug = (spec.get("github") or spec["gitea"]) if spec else arg if "/" in arg else "cartwmic/" + arg
    gitea = {v["gitea"].lower() for v in REPOS.values() if v and "gitea" in v}
    return slug, slug.lower() in gitea


def thread_lines(slug, pr, found):
    if not found:
        return [f"{slug}#{pr}: GREEN  no unresolved review threads"]
    lines = [f"{slug}#{pr}: RED  {len(found)} unresolved review thread{'s' if len(found) != 1 else ''}: resolve each, or say why it stays, before merging"]
    return lines + [f"    {t['where']}  {t['text']}  {t['url']}" for t in found]


def threads_log_path():
    return Path(os.environ.get("CI_MAIN_STATUS_THREADS_LOG")
                or Path(os.environ.get("XDG_STATE_HOME") or Path.home() / ".local/state") / "ci-main-status/threads.jsonl")


def log_threads(slug, pr, forge, started, code, found, error):
    """One JSON line per --threads run, whoever calls it (the shim, the Gitea gate, a person): the repo, PR and forge, the result (pass, refused or
    error), the unresolved threads, the exit code and, on error, why. A log that cannot be written is a stderr note and never changes the verdict."""
    detail = error or ""
    if _TOKEN and _TOKEN[0]:
        detail = detail.replace(_TOKEN[0], "<token>")
    row = {"ts": datetime.datetime.fromtimestamp(started, datetime.timezone.utc).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ"),
           "duration_ms": round((time.time() - started) * 1000), "repo": slug, "pr": pr, "forge": forge,
           "result": "error" if error else "refused" if found else "pass", "unresolved": None if error else len(found),
           "threads": [{"where": t["where"], "url": t["url"]} for t in found or []], "exit": code, "detail": detail[:300]}
    try:
        path = threads_log_path()
        path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        with open(path, "a") as f:
            f.write(json.dumps(row) + "\n")
    except OSError as e:
        print(f"ci-main-status: could not write {threads_log_path()}: {e}", file=sys.stderr)


def check_threads(arg, pr):
    """One PR's review threads: (exit code, lines). A read that fails is ERROR, exit 1. Every call leaves one line in threads.jsonl."""
    slug, on_gitea = thread_repo(arg)
    started = time.time()
    found, error = [], None
    try:
        found = (gitea_threads if on_gitea else github_threads)(slug, pr)
        code, lines = (1 if found else 0), thread_lines(slug, pr, found)
    except Unreadable as e:
        error = str(e)
        code, lines = 1, [f"{slug}#{pr}: ERROR  cannot read review threads: {e}"]
    log_threads(slug, pr, "gitea" if on_gitea else "github", started, code, found, error)
    return code, lines


def check(name, tip_only=False, pr=None, gate=False, rec=None):
    spec = REPOS[name]
    if spec is None:
        return 0, [f"{name}: n/a (gate is per-PR only)"]
    if spec.get("no_ci"):
        return no_ci(name, spec, tip_only, pr, gate)
    if "gitea" in spec:
        return gitea_check(name, spec, tip_only, pr, gate, rec if rec is not None else {})
    if "journal" in spec:
        verdicts, going = journal_verdicts()
    else:
        verdicts, going = github_verdicts(spec)
    trees = passing_trees(verdicts) if "journal" in spec else None
    code, lines = assess(name, spec["github"], verdicts, going, "journal line" if "journal" in spec else "run", tip_only, trees, spec, pr)
    if "journal" in spec and not verdicts:
        lines.insert(0, f"  (no journal record at {JOURNAL})")
    return code, lines


def gitea_log_path():
    return Path(os.environ.get("CI_MAIN_STATUS_GITEA_LOG")
                or Path(os.environ.get("XDG_STATE_HOME") or Path.home() / ".local/state") / "ci-main-status/gitea.jsonl")


GITEA_VERDICT = re.compile(r"^[^:]+: (GREEN|RED|UNTESTED|ERROR)\b")


def log_gitea(name, spec, action, pr, started, code, lines, rec):
    """One JSON line per budget-steward call, kept after the terminal is gone: UTC time, duration, action (merge-gate, tip or status),
    repo, PR, sha, tree, verdict, exit code and the evidence it used (Gitea status state and kgate job id, or none). `exit` is the
    gate's own code; the token is never in it. A log that cannot be written is a stderr note and never changes the verdict."""
    out = "\n".join(lines)
    token = _TOKEN[0] if _TOKEN else None
    if token:
        out = out.replace(token, "<token>")
    m = GITEA_VERDICT.match(lines[0]) if lines else None
    row = {"ts": datetime.datetime.fromtimestamp(started, datetime.timezone.utc).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ"),
           "duration_ms": round((time.time() - started) * 1000), "action": action, "repo": spec["gitea"], "pr": pr or None,
           "sha": rec.get("sha"), "tree": rec.get("tree"), "verdict": m.group(1) if m else "ERROR", "exit": code,
           "evidence": rec.get("evidence"), "detail": out.splitlines()[0][:300] if out else ""}
    try:
        path = gitea_log_path()
        path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        with open(path, "a") as f:
            f.write(json.dumps(row) + "\n")
    except OSError as e:
        print(f"ci-main-status: could not write {gitea_log_path()}: {e}", file=sys.stderr)


def describe(name, tip_only=False, pr=None, gate=False):
    """Run one repo. A state it cannot read is one ERROR line and exit 1; the other repos still run."""
    spec = REPOS[name]
    rec = {}
    started = time.time()
    try:
        code, lines = check(name, tip_only, pr, gate, rec)
    except Unreadable as e:
        code, lines = 1, [f"{name}: ERROR  cannot read state: {e}"]
    except Exception as e:   # a shape gh did not promise: one line on stdout, the traceback on stderr
        traceback.print_exc(file=sys.stderr)
        code, lines = 1, [f"{name}: ERROR  cannot read state: unexpected {type(e).__name__}: {e}"]
    if spec and "gitea" in spec:
        log_gitea(name, spec, "merge-gate" if gate else "tip" if tip_only else "status", pr if gate else None, started, code, lines, rec)
    return code, lines


def main(argv):
    global URGENT
    if "--threads" in argv:
        rest = [a for a in argv if a != "--threads"]
        if len(rest) != 2 or not rest[1].isdigit() or int(rest[1]) < 1 or rest[0].startswith("-"):
            print("usage: ci-main-status --threads REPO PR     (REPO: a table name, OWNER/REPO, or NAME for cartwmic/NAME)", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        URGENT = True   # a merge-chain read: the gh budget guard must not refuse it
        code, lines = check_threads(rest[0], int(rest[1]))
        print("\n".join(lines))
        return code
    tip_only = "--tip" in argv
    merge_gate = "--merge-gate" in argv
    URGENT = tip_only or merge_gate
    argv = [a for a in argv if a not in ("--tip", "--merge-gate")]
    by_slug = {(v.get("github") or v["gitea"]).lower(): k for k, v in REPOS.items() if v}
    argv = [by_slug.get(a.lower(), a) for a in argv]   # every table repo's OWNER/REPO is its table entry: the any-repo path reads only GitHub's required checks, a weaker gate than the table's whole-run read
    pr = None
    if "--pr" in argv:
        k = argv.index("--pr")
        value = argv[k + 1] if k + 1 < len(argv) else ""
        pr = int(value) if value.isdigit() and int(value) > 0 else 0
        del argv[k:k + 2]
        if not pr or not merge_gate or tip_only or len(argv) != 1 or (argv[0] not in REPOS and "/" not in argv[0]):
            argv = []   # --pr needs a PR number, --merge-gate and one repo (not --all): usage error
    if tip_only and merge_gate:
        argv = []   # the two flags disagree about UNTESTED: usage error
    if argv == ["--all"]:
        names = ORDER
    elif len(argv) == 1 and argv[0] in REPOS:
        names = argv
    elif len(argv) == 1 and "/" in argv[0] and not tip_only:
        names = argv   # OWNER/REPO: a GitHub repo not in the table; --tip is not for these repos
    else:
        print(__doc__.split("\n\n")[0] + "\n\nusage: ci-main-status [--tip | --merge-gate] REPO | [--tip | --merge-gate] --all | --merge-gate REPO --pr N | [--merge-gate] OWNER/REPO [--pr N] | --threads REPO PR  (REPO: dotfiles, loop-engine, agent-kit, coordinator, homelab, amazon-itemizer, alert-steward, storycraft, retro, eval-cases, budget-steward)", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    rank = {0: 0, 2: 1, 1: 2}   # 1 beats 2 beats 0
    worst = 0
    for name in names:
        if name in REPOS:
            code, lines = describe(name, tip_only, pr, merge_gate and len(names) == 1)
        else:
            code, lines = describe_any(name, pr)
        print("\n".join(lines))
        if rank[code] > rank[worst]:
            worst = code
    # UNTESTED passes the merge gate only for the table repos (main is not red). For OWNER/REPO a pending, missing
    # or never-reported required check never passes it (lead decision, 2026-11-18): non-zero either way.
    return 0 if merge_gate and worst == 2 and names[0] in REPOS else worst


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
